@{ ViewData["Title"] = "How it works"; }
<section class="pub-page-top container"><p class="pub-kicker">GETTING STARTED</p><h1>Your exam,<br /><em>step by step.</em></h1><p class="pub-lead">Start with the guide for your role. Keep the checklist nearby before your first examination.</p><nav class="pub-jump" aria-label="Choose a guide"><a href="#students">For students ↓</a><a href="#teachers">For teachers ↓</a><a href="#checklist">Before-exam checklist ↓</a></nav></section>
<section id="students" class="pub-section container pub-guide"><div><p class="pub-kicker">01 / STUDENTS</p><h2>From signing in<br />to submitting.</h2><a class="pub-text-link" asp-area="Student" asp-controller="Dashboard" asp-action="Index">Open the student portal →</a></div><ol class="pub-steps"><li><strong>Sign in and find your exam</strong><p>Check the scheduled date and entry window. If the exam is missing, ask your teacher to check your assignment or eligibility.</p></li><li><strong>Read the rules and complete setup</strong><p>Follow the identity and device checks. Allow the camera and microphone when requested. If screen monitoring is required, choose the requested display in the browser's sharing dialog.</p></li><li><strong>Start and work through the questions</strong><p>Enter fullscreen when required. Use the question navigation, watch the timer and check the answer-saving status. Follow any instructions shown during monitoring.</p></li><li><strong>Review and submit</strong><p>Check unanswered or marked questions, then submit the session. For exams with multiple sessions, follow the break and continuation instructions.</p></li><li><strong>Find your result</strong><p>Open My Results when your teacher releases the result. A submitted attempt may still be waiting for review.</p></li></ol></section>
<section id="teachers" class="pub-section pub-tinted"><div class="container pub-guide"><div><p class="pub-kicker">02 / TEACHERS</p><h2>Prepare the test.<br />Follow the attempt.</h2><a class="pub-text-link" asp-area="Teacher" asp-controller="Dashboard" asp-action="Index">Open the teacher portal →</a></div><ol class="pub-steps"><li><strong>Complete account approval</strong><p>Register as a teacher and wait for administrator approval before accessing teaching tools.</p></li><li><strong>Create and configure the exam</strong><p>Add questions, marks, sessions and timing. Choose candidate access, monitoring categories, warning limits and blocking rules carefully.</p></li><li><strong>Publish and share entry instructions</strong><p>Check the candidate list and schedule. Explain device requirements and how students can reach you if setup fails.</p></li><li><strong>Monitor and review</strong><p>Use live monitoring and alerts during attempts. Review available evidence and handle pause, resume and result decisions through your authorised tools.</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section id="checklist" class="pub-section container pub-split"><div><p class="pub-kicker">BEFORE EXAM DAY</p><h2>A little preparation<br />makes a difference.</h2><p>Use the browser and device recommended by your examination organiser. Complete the system's own checks before starting.</p></div><ul class="pub-checklist"><li>Confirm the exam date, time and entry window.</li><li>Keep your sign-in details and Candidate ID ready.</li><li>Charge your device and check the internet connection.</li><li>Use a quiet space with enough light for your camera.</li><li>Check camera, microphone and any required screen-sharing permissions.</li><li>Keep your teacher's contact details available.</li></ul></section>
<section class="container pub-help-bar"><div><h2>Stuck at one of the steps?</h2><p>Find guidance for common setup and examination problems.</p></div><a class="pub-button" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Contact">Open the help guide →</a></section>